WEBVTT

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:10.590
Wiping off my tears.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:13.300
I'm starting to run now

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:18.560
Tomorrow I'll be born anew.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:24.370
How could "you always be my friend"?

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:29.280
That person's word makes me more courageous.

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:33.480
There are times when it's possible I will be depressed

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:38.580
and there are times when things are delightful.

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:45.170
I'll always be

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:51.020
next to you.

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:55.910
Smiling 100%

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:59.450
Striking 100%

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:03.640
I've come so far.

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:06.560
Being 100% pure

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:10.190
The things I want to tell you

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:14.670
change to treasure completely.

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:17.190
in the 100% case

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:20.950
Even if it's a long distance,

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:27.280
I'll still say I would meet you with the same feelings.

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:38.010
You mean he’s a runaway?!

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:40.760
Well, Mom, it’s kind of complicated.

00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:43.180
Ryuu-kun, calm down and think about this.

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:48.610
I don’t know what happened, but your parents will be worried about you.

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:51.820
I don’t have any parents to worry.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:57.570
My parents passed away when I was an infant.

00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:03.410
Since childhood, I’ve been raised by virtual strangers.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:05.790
It’s as if I'm their prisoner.

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:13.670
Not only that, but I've been ordered to pretend
that the person caring for me is my mother.

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:16.010
Ordered’? By whom?

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:18.180
By my grandfather.

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:20.140
Why would your grandfather do that?

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:22.260
I'm sorry, Kyuu,

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:24.060
can that wait for another time?

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:27.770
When the time comes, I'll tell you the truth myself.

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:28.980
I promise you.

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:34.400
I understand.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:37.200
It seems like you have some complicated issues to work out.

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:41.070
If you're really in trouble, then you should stay with us.

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:44.120
With Ryuu-kun here, things will certainly be more exciting, won't they?

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:45.660
Mom!

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.960
Thank you so much.

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:52.290
Alright then, we've got to celebrate Ryuu-kun’s arrival.

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:54.300
I'll cook a feast for all of...

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:57.050
Oh! I forgot to go shopping!

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:07.520
Mom, isn’t this enough?

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:09.640
We have so much already.

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:13.980
Well, the store on third street is having a three-for-one sale on eggs.

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:16.940
The limit's one package per person, so we all have to go.

00:03:16.970 --> 00:03:20.280
Oh, sorry for making you come along too, Ryuu-kun.

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:20.950
It's nothing.

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:25.910
But, you know, I hear it comes out on Third street.

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:26.490
What comes out?

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:29.080
The Headless Woman of the Maze.

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:30.170
A headless woman?

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:36.000
On Third street, in a creepy area, there are lots of old, decaying houses.

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:42.510
The third bock up here was made to avoid Jizo statues and
small shrines, the high walls wind around like a maze.

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:51.100
They say that in this maze of roads, the Headless Woman appears at night.

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:54.310
Surely that’s just a rumor.

00:03:54.590 --> 00:03:57.980
But Takahashi-san from across the street says she saw it!

00:03:58.010 --> 00:04:00.530
She’s not one to make things up, either.

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:03.240
It sure is scary.

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:04.950
Are you hoping to see to, Mom?

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:09.200
Wow, this sure seems like an old district.

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:11.580
There are hardly any street lights.

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:14.170
It must be awfully dark and scary at night.

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:19.800
Not only that, but it’s mostly abandoned houses
after this, so there’s almost no one about.

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:23.590
It isn't far from the station, so it's odd that they should be empty.

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:25.550
Well, it was pretty sudden.

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:27.560
I suppose the bubble just burst.

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:30.850
It really does have a creepy atmosphere about It.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:46.740
Kyuu, what’s the matter?

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:47.410
Let’s go.

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:49.120
Ah, yeah.

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:55.830
Did you see something, Kyuu?

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:58.170
Ah, no, I guess it was just my imagination.

00:04:58.190 --> 00:04:59.750
Oh.

00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:01.720
What was with that girl?

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:03.260
Where are you off to?

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:07.550
You'd be better off not going any further.

00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:09.930
Something might really come out

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:11.890
Have you seen it too, Ma'am?

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:13.640
Without a doubt!

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:17.520
It was the Headless Woman!

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:22.690
For a long time, this has been a strange place.

00:05:22.930 --> 00:05:28.580
Back when they were planning to mace this into a
resident al area, they tried to move many shrines.

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:32.290
Various people met with mysterious accidents afterwards.

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:35.170
This lot is cursed.

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:39.880
They say that if you see the headless woman
more than once, your fate i sealed.

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:43.210
It would be best for you not to go near there.

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:44.590
Hurry home.

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:52.020
I just remembered: that sale on eggs was yesterday!

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:53.680
I’m such an airhead!

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:54.560
Let's go home!

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:55.560
I'll check it out.

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:58.520
I want to see for myself if the Headless Woman is real.

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:00.400
W-What are you talking about?

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:02.230
You were so scared a minute ago.

00:06:02.260 --> 00:06:03.740
You'll come home, won’t you, Ryuu-kun?

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:05.200
I'm sorry.

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:06.200
I'd like to investigate as well.

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:14.120
It's totally dark, isn’t it?

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:16.830
Oh, over there.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:31.010
They say that the Headless Woman comes over
that hill and heads to the left into the maze.

00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:35.480
We ll, it could happen like this:

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:43.730
That branch over there hangs over the road, so from here,
it would be at the perfect height to obstruct someone’s head.

00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:49.610
But in that case, wouldn't we see the person's head
after she came out from behind the branch?

00:06:50.140 --> 00:06:54.950
Once a person gets an idea in there head, it can be difficult to grasp the truth.

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:58.920
It wouldn’t be unreasonable for someone who had
heard the rumor to be scared out of their wits,

00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:01.170
after seeing something like that in the dark.

00:07:05.990 --> 00:07:08.550
W-What's the matter, Ryuu-kun?

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:10.050
The wind’s picking up again.

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:22.560
It sure is eerie.

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:34.910
Even though it’s winter, there’s a wind chime out?

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:41.540
Now that you mention it, the headless woman has a lantern
in her right hand, and a wind chime in her left.

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:42.290
It’s coming from the hill.

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:45.550
It cant be.

00:07:45.570 --> 00:07:47.090
Is that light from a lantern?

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:49.420
I thought she only appeared late at night.

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:52.840
Those footsteps sound like sandals.

00:07:52.870 --> 00:07:54.220
She’s in Japanese attire.

00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:57.890
We must cam down.

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:01.480
If my theory is indeed correct, we should be able to see it
for what it is after it comes out from behind the branch.

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:16.410
It’s the Headless Woman!

00:08:28.030 --> 00:08:28.960
Kyuu, where are you going?

00:08:29.450 --> 00:08:31.420
I'm going to follow it and find out who t really s!

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:32.630
Alright, I'll go too.

00:08:32.660 --> 00:08:34.430
H-hey, you two, wait for me!

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:39.520
She’s not here.

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:40.560
Where could she have gone?

00:08:42.040 --> 00:08:43.850
It’s coming from over there

00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:45.270
The maze is in that direction.

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:45.770
Let’s go!

00:08:49.010 --> 00:08:50.190
It’s a dead end.

00:08:50.220 --> 00:08:51.490
No, this way!

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:53.200
Wow, it’s so dark, I can’t tell.

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:56.570
Where is she?

00:09:00.980 --> 00:09:04.460
Damn! It’s a single path, but it really is like a maze.

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:07.250
But still, how can she be so fast?

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:09.590
No matter how much we turn, we aren’t catching up.

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:11.880
There! The chiming stopped.

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:13.170
Alright!

00:09:14.910 --> 00:09:16.090
Stop right there!

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:20.560
She’s not there.

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:22.060
And it’s a dead end, to boot.

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:24.390
I can’t believe it!

00:09:24.420 --> 00:09:26.730
There wasn’t a fork in the road, or ever a door.

00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:30.400
Also, until just a moment ago, we could hear the sounds of the wind chime.

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:32.690
Let’s take a look.

00:09:36.890 --> 00:09:40.240
That’s the lantern that the Headless Woman was carrying.

00:09:40.270 --> 00:09:42.000
Where did she go after leaving this here?

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:45.120
The door looks like it’s nailed shut

00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:49.500
At this height, it'd be impossible to scale the
fence in such a short amount of time.

00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:54.420
There are holes at the bottom, but there’s no
way she could fit into such a tight space

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:57.010
So do you think she really disappeared?

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:08.520
The wax is hard

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:11.230
The wax is?

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:12.150
Who's there?

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:13.150
Whatever is the matter?

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:17.360
Oh, it’s just the old lady from before

00:10:20.810 --> 00:10:22.950
Is there something wrong with that girl?

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:24.120
You can see her too, Mom?

00:10:24.140 --> 00:10:26.960
What do you mean, “can you see her?”

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:31.290
This is Makoto-chan.

00:10:31.320 --> 00:10:34.050
She used to live around here, and still comes quite often to walk her dog.

00:10:34.070 --> 00:10:38.430
We were standing there talking, so we decided
to see what all the noise was about.

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:42.140
You weren't looking for the Headless Woman, were you?

00:10:42.330 --> 00:10:45.220
Of course not! Why would we...

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:48.480
Oh, Ma’am, are you a bit slimmer than you were this afternoon?

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:50.560
What are you doing? That's rude.

00:10:50.590 --> 00:10:55.230
Oh, well I was just coming back from a friend's
house, so was wearing a kimono.

00:10:55.260 --> 00:10:57.280
You look fatter when wearing a kimono?

00:11:00.390 --> 00:11:05.700
Well , when you wear a kimono, if you don’t pad
the front, you look something of a floozy

00:11:05.730 --> 00:11:13.540
So, old lady that am, I pit a towel in there to pad myself up.

00:11:13.570 --> 00:11:19.010
Well , I suppose young people’s mothers don’t wear
kimonos, so you wouldn’t know that, would you?

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:20.720
Well, I feel like should apologize.

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:25.430
Well, Makoto-chan’s mother was always so well dressed.

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:28.810
She was so young but always took the trouble to look her best.

00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:37.320
Oh, I’m sorry, it's all right.

00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:39.400
I'm sure your mother will be home soon..

00:11:42.600 --> 00:11:44.830
After all that, we end up, eating instant ramen huh?

00:11:45.310 --> 00:11:49.790
Sorry Ryuu, in all that commotion back there we forgot the grocery bags.

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:53.790
We ll, my mom’s always busy, so I’m pretty used to this.

00:11:56.610 --> 00:11:58.130
Oh! Ryuu, it hasn’t been three minutes yet.

00:11:58.150 --> 00:11:58.590
Huh?

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:01.800
Could it be that you've never eaten this?

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:06.350
No. Everything a normal child would do was always forbidden to me.

00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:16.190
Toys, tantrums, paying outside and even the chance to make any friends.

00:12:29.310 --> 00:12:30.830
Kyuu, what’s the matter?

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:35.590
Oh, I was thinking about when was a kid.

00:12:35.610 --> 00:12:36.880
You mean about your father?

00:12:40.650 --> 00:12:44.680
Ever since I can remember, my father hasn’t been around.

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:45.680
And, one day, my mother...

00:12:46.830 --> 00:12:48.470
Mommy!

00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:51.350
Why don't fave a father?

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:54.190
Where’s my father?

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:03.700
Ever since then, I’ve ever been able to ask her.

00:13:11.730 --> 00:13:13.500
Kyuu...

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:18.460
It's about time.

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:19.750
I wonder if it'll appear?

00:13:19.780 --> 00:13:20.760
It will appear.

00:13:20.780 --> 00:13:21.460
I'm sure of It.

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:24.220
There’s a trick, for sure

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:25.680
Don’t you think so, Ryuu?

00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:29.180
M-Mom!

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:31.600
You came here today too, did you?

00:13:31.620 --> 00:13:35.350
N-No. We came here to pick up the groceries from yesterday.

00:13:35.380 --> 00:13:37.810
And, did you find them?

00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:42.530
Aren’t they over there, picked apart by the crows?

00:13:43.180 --> 00:13:45.530
Goodness, you’re a bad liar.

00:13:45.550 --> 00:13:49.030
You know, they say that if you see the Headless Woman twice, you'll die!

00:13:49.060 --> 00:13:50.870
What'll you do if it appears again?

00:13:51.060 --> 00:13:53.000
Surely that’s just lie!

00:13:53.020 --> 00:13:55.750
But, she didn’t have a head, and she disappeared too!

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:57.420
Surely she’s a real ghost.

00:13:57.440 --> 00:14:01.090
You say that she disappeared, but it's not like we saw her doing it.

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:02.760
We , I suppose, but...

00:14:03.150 --> 00:14:04.090
There are three hints.

00:14:04.990 --> 00:14:11.760
The first is whether or not the Headless Woman really went into the maze.

00:14:11.790 --> 00:14:15.270
The second is the reason for the old lady’s weight loss.

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:19.020
And the third is the hardened wax on the candle.

00:14:19.340 --> 00:14:22.150
There is only one answer!

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:32.910
We , it should be about time.

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:36.710
Yes, but there’s no wind chime to be heard.

00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:39.580
I-I suppose today’s her day off.

00:14:41.230 --> 00:14:41.670
Here she comes.

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:48.970
Let's run before she comes into sight.

00:14:49.410 --> 00:14:50.470
Too late!

00:14:55.250 --> 00:14:56.600
You two, don't look!

00:14:56.620 --> 00:14:58.640
You'll die if you see her a second t me

00:14:58.670 --> 00:15:00.520
Please, please see me through this.

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:05.110
Namuamidabu, Namuamidabu, Namuamidabuuu...

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:05.940
Alright! Let’s go!

00:15:06.930 --> 00:15:07.900
Wait for me!

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:13.160
Wait!

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:14.620
What is it?

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:15.660
Let's wait here.

00:15:15.680 --> 00:15:16.950
What's going on?

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:18.290
A scream?

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:19.040
Now!

00:15:19.060 --> 00:15:20.420
You too Mom, quickly!

00:15:28.110 --> 00:15:29.430
There’s two headless people!

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:33.970
Hey, you can take that off now.

00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:43.730
Just because, as the successor to the Natusawa household,
I've been taught how to dress traditionally.

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:46.480
I've never dressed up like this before.

00:15:46.510 --> 00:15:47.740
A costume!

00:15:47.760 --> 00:15:50.070
This is the trick behind the headless people.

00:15:51.010 --> 00:15:55.370
The old lady used padding to make herself look less slender,

00:16:01.360 --> 00:16:06.300
§o, in other words, you can’t use this trick without a small child.

00:16:06.320 --> 00:16:08.510
Isn’t that right, Ms. Headless Woman?

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:17.970
Makoto-chan!

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:22.770
You learned how to wear a kimono from your
mother, a traditional dress teacher, right?

00:16:23.340 --> 00:16:25.310
That’s how you were able to think up this trick.

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:30.650
But, in that case, how could she appear and disappear like that?

00:16:30.680 --> 00:16:32.240
The key to that is the sound of the wind chime.

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:33.070
The sound of the wind chime?

00:16:33.600 --> 00:16:34.450
That's right.

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:38.080
When it's completely dark, people tend to
use the sounds around them to navigate

00:16:38.730 --> 00:16:45.250
In other words, we unconscious y followed the sound of the
wind chime in an attempt to follow the headless woman.

00:16:45.860 --> 00:16:49.760
So, we were drawn into the maze, all the way to the dead end.

00:16:50.780 --> 00:16:56.970
In truth, however, she did not actually go into
the maze, but rather, hide in the shadows.

00:16:57.370 --> 00:17:01.230
To prove that, I came here in disguise.

00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:04.940
Then, what on earth was the wind chime sound that we followed?

00:17:07.300 --> 00:17:10.320
No way! There’s another headless person?

00:17:10.340 --> 00:17:11.240
Not at all.

00:17:20.270 --> 00:17:23.250
That's the puppy that was with Makoto-chan!

00:17:23.270 --> 00:17:23.870
That's right.

00:17:24.650 --> 00:17:31.840
When she came to the maze, she had the dog put a wind chime
in its mouth, and timed her escape to coincide with our arrival.

00:17:32.490 --> 00:17:37.800
Also, such a small puppy would easily be able
to fit through the holes underneath the door.

00:17:44.670 --> 00:17:49.860
Makoto-chan, in order to make it appear as
though the Headless Woman disappeared,

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:52.150
you hung a lantern from the door at the end of the line.

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:57.570
However, the wax of the candle, which was supposed to
have been burning up until a moment before, was solid.

00:17:57.600 --> 00:17:58.820
That’s when the idea struck me.

00:18:04.190 --> 00:18:08.210
You know, Makoto-chan, if you had gone any
further with this, it would have been a crime.

00:18:08.230 --> 00:18:09.420
What would make you...

00:18:09.440 --> 00:18:10.420
Idiot!

00:18:10.650 --> 00:18:13.420
My mother’s home is going to disappear!

00:18:19.370 --> 00:18:23.350
Makoto-chan, these people haven't done anything wrong, have they?

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:24.560
Ma’am!

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:25.850
Well, well.

00:18:25.870 --> 00:18:28.980
To think that Makoto-chan was the Headless Woman.

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:33.030
It's mostly empty buildings around here, so
I could hear you all from a mile away.

00:18:33.300 --> 00:18:42.450
She lived together with her mother in one of the buildings
near the maze, but one day her mother just went missing.

00:18:42.470 --> 00:18:47.750
Her uncle took her in, but he wanted to sell that house.

00:18:48.020 --> 00:18:52.960
§o, that’s why you made up the Headless Woman
so they wouldn’t be able to demolish the houses around here.

00:18:54.530 --> 00:18:57.090
She’s really a nice, bright young girl.

00:18:57.110 --> 00:19:07.890
She grew somewhat bitter after having her father die, her
mother abandon her, and her childhood home a most sold.

00:19:11.590 --> 00:19:14.730
My mother wouldn’t just abandon me!

00:19:14.760 --> 00:19:17.440
My uncle says she isn’t coming back, but that’s definitely a lie!

00:19:18.430 --> 00:19:20.660
I'm sure that something happened to her!

00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:23.620
She wants to come home, but can’t for some reason.

00:19:23.640 --> 00:19:28.910
But, if my house is gone, there won't be anywhere for her to come home to.

00:19:29.270 --> 00:19:33.380
The house where my father died, my mother’s house...

00:19:48.960 --> 00:19:50.940
Makoto-chan, let’s look for her.

00:19:51.380 --> 00:19:52.520
Kyuu!

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:57.400
My father died when I was young too.

00:19:57.970 --> 00:20:00.900
So, I know how you feel.

00:20:00.930 --> 00:20:01.860
Oni-chan!

00:20:02.220 --> 00:20:05.830
After all, if my mom were to disappear, it'd be hard on me too.

00:20:06.430 --> 00:20:08.540
So, let’s look for her

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:11.790
I'll be sure to find your mother, Makoto-chan!

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:15.250
Let me help too.

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:16.630
Ryuu!

00:20:16.650 --> 00:20:18.590
I'll help too.

00:20:18.610 --> 00:20:22.260
If I can’t find a missing person,I have no right to call myself a detective.

00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:23.760
Kazuma!

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:25.300
You see, Makoto-chan?

00:20:25.330 --> 00:20:28.140
They'll all help you find your mother.

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:30.480
So cheer up, Makoto-chan

00:20:38.470 --> 00:20:39.860
Alright!

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:42.490
DDS is the best!

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:43.280
We did it, Ryuu!

00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:44.070
Right!

00:20:45.470 --> 00:20:47.660
Mom! We did it! We did it!

00:20:50.270 --> 00:20:52.710
Mom, it’s me, it’s me!

00:20:52.730 --> 00:20:53.420
Kyuu!

00:20:53.440 --> 00:20:54.790
That's going a little far, Kyuu.

00:20:55.150 --> 00:20:56.420
What's the natter, Kyuu?

00:20:56.440 --> 00:20:57.250
What happened?

00:20:57.530 --> 00:20:58.880
We found her:

00:20:58.900 --> 00:21:00.340
Makoto-chan’s mother!

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:01.800
Really?

00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:06.600
We looked up Makoto-chan’s mother in DDS’s missing persons list.

00:21:06.620 --> 00:21:12.060
When we looked for people matching her description in the area,

00:21:12.080 --> 00:21:16.610
we found a woman who'd been hospitalized
after losing her memory in an accident.

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:18.610
Lost her memory?

00:21:18.630 --> 00:21:21.610
So, she didn’t know where she was?

00:21:21.630 --> 00:21:24.110
Oh, then, I suppose she didn’t remember Makoto-chan, either.

00:21:24.760 --> 00:21:25.160
Well , about that...

00:21:29.470 --> 00:21:33.000
When we showed her a picture, she remembered Makoto-chan...

00:21:33.310 --> 00:21:34.120
Really?

00:21:35.360 --> 00:21:42.170
Not only that, but the doctors said that her home would be the best pace
for her to recover her memories, so she's being released tomorrow.

00:21:42.530 --> 00:21:44.260
Then, they'll be together tomorrow?

00:21:44.280 --> 00:21:44.630
Yes!

00:21:44.990 --> 00:21:46.840
Alright!

00:21:46.870 --> 00:21:48.220
How nice for then.

00:21:48.240 --> 00:21:52.890
After all, Makoto-chan went through all that to protect her mother’s home.

00:21:54.620 --> 00:21:56.690
But, it’s too bad, Mom.

00:21:56.710 --> 00:21:57.600
What?

00:21:57.630 --> 00:22:00.070
Too bad the Headless Woman wasn't a real ghost.

00:22:00.510 --> 00:22:01.650
Idiot!

00:22:01.670 --> 00:22:04.360
It’s a good thing that it wasn’t a real ghost

00:22:04.380 --> 00:22:07.030
If it had been real, you’d have died after seeing it that second it time.

00:22:11.470 --> 00:22:13.870
Do you realize how worried I was?!

00:22:13.890 --> 00:22:15.000
I'm sorry.

00:22:15.020 --> 00:22:16.120
You too, Ryuu-kun.

00:22:21.690 --> 00:22:25.510
I never know what kind of trouble you're going
to get into, so you have to take care!

00:22:25.530 --> 00:22:26.760
I'm sorry.

00:22:26.780 --> 00:22:27.090
Huh?

00:22:28.320 --> 00:22:31.050
Why are we having such a feast tonight?

00:22:36.830 --> 00:22:39.730
I'll warm up the soup. You two go wash your hands.

00:22:43.090 --> 00:22:45.490
She was really worried about me.

00:22:46.260 --> 00:22:49.950
How nice. Mother, huh?

00:22:53.480 --> 00:22:54.120
Hello?

00:22:55.440 --> 00:22:57.040
Have you had any contact with Ryuu-sama?

00:22:57.060 --> 00:22:59.500
No, I have not, Sir Anubis.

00:22:59.520 --> 00:23:02.630
Wouldn’t it be best for the other members to go and retrieve him?

00:23:03.030 --> 00:23:04.840
There’s no need.

00:23:04.860 --> 00:23:07.550
We'll eventually get a report from Echidna.

00:23:08.070 --> 00:23:09.260
Echidna?

00:23:09.280 --> 00:23:11.050
You mean the spy we've sent to DDS?

00:23:11.370 --> 00:23:13.760
There’s no need for you to know that information.

00:23:13.790 --> 00:23:16.350
Just hold your position and what for for Ryuu-sama.

00:23:38.980 --> 00:23:39.830
Darling.

00:23:40.650 --> 00:23:43.380
Kyuu has grown up.

00:23:47.860 --> 00:23:51.770
Somehow it's collapsing

00:23:51.800 --> 00:23:54.140
Embracing such a feeling.

00:23:54.160 --> 00:23:55.030
Flowing.

00:23:55.050 --> 00:23:58.910
I'd be worried tomorrow.

00:23:58.930 --> 00:24:01.120
If the same thing happened.

00:24:01.140 --> 00:24:02.120
Go wrong.

00:24:02.130 --> 00:24:06.460
He looks up at the sky, pondering

00:24:06.470 --> 00:24:09.020
You're very far away.

00:24:09.930 --> 00:24:13.180
Show your heart if you have the courage

00:24:13.190 --> 00:24:16.310
passing the border line.

00:24:16.330 --> 00:24:19.760
In order to get past, I walk against the wind

00:24:19.770 --> 00:24:23.400
and I can finish a battle.

00:24:23.420 --> 00:24:26.940
When I feel like an abandoned child

00:24:26.970 --> 00:24:30.360
then I'll stand in line with you.

00:24:30.390 --> 00:24:33.930
Facing the wind, I forget,

00:24:33.940 --> 00:24:37.540
somehow this is the only important thing.

00:24:37.550 --> 00:24:40.290
We protect, because there Is no return.

00:24:40.310 --> 00:24:41.890
It's becoming dearly.

00:24:41.920 --> 00:24:45.840
Today I embrace, right now I conquer.

00:24:47.090 --> 00:24:58.490
Next Episode

00:24:47.550 --> 00:24:50.280
A body is found in a secret room surrounded by concrete.

00:24:50.300 --> 00:24:53.200
The legendary princess Maya who protects the vanishing city.

00:24:53.220 --> 00:24:56.120
The flames of that curse burn at the intruder.

00:24:56.140 --> 00:24:58.450
Those who want to protect the village, those who want to abandon it.

00:25:02.100 --> 00:25:04.000
Who's the real traitor?

00:25:04.020 --> 00:25:06.710
There is only one answer!

00:25:07.480 --> 00:25:09.210
Tadaaa!

00:25:10.190 --> 00:25:12.590
Ryuu, were you surprised?

00:25:12.610 --> 00:25:16.970
Kyuu, that won’t be funny forever.

00:25:16.990 --> 00:25:18.560
Oh, see

00:25:18.580 --> 00:25:19.850
How disappointing

00:25:19.870 --> 00:25:20.970
Well, that’s a bit funny, there.
